Notes another track's plugins hear (Segno: docs/design/midi-effects.md §5.3, a MIDI effect's Listen).

A plugin may name a track whose notes it hears apart from its own (Plugin::getNoteSourceID).
That track then sends its notes on a bus of their own from before its first plugin that takes
notes and isn't a note effect (Plugin::isNoteEffect): after its MIDI effects, before its
instrument, which may pass no notes on (a Drum Kit's rack). Before the hearing plugin's own
node, a NoteSourceNode hands it that block's notes (Plugin::setSourceNotes) and passes its input
on unchanged, so the notes never mix with the track's own. A muted track others hear still
plays its notes for them, silently, as a sidechain source does. With none named, nothing
changes.

